{
  "_note": [
    "Transcribed from player_aid/LoH_Campaign_Season_Sheet.pdf. Round counts",
    "and event card ids are exact transcriptions of the 'Sequence of Rounds'",
    "and 'Event Cards' columns. Card TEXT/effects are not stored anywhere —",
    "only the ids, since the app treats cards as physical and the player",
    "reads them at the table.",
    "",
    "CS X and CS XII: onCampaignRounds is 2 by the booklet's own rule ('CS X",
    "and XII: ... 2 Rounds' — worded to apply whether or not any Grognard is",
    "actually assigned to Spain), even though the sheet's own 'Sequence of",
    "Rounds' column only prints one 'X-#?' placeholder per season for the",
    "Spain-exclusive extra round(s); flags.spainBattleRounds marks these two",
    "seasons. Card ids 'X-#a'/'X-#b' and 'XII-#a'/'XII-#b' are this app's own",
    "split of that single printed placeholder into two slots — the sheet",
    "does not print two distinct ids, so treat these two ids as provisional.",
    "",
    "CS I's sheet entry literally reads '(no Campaign Season Segment) I-1,",
    "I-2, I-A, I-B' — the only season without a Segment, matching the",
    "booklet's 'not for CS I'.",
    "",
    "CS XVI's On Campaign round XVI-A contains four cards played in forced",
    "succession (Ligny, then Quatre Bras/Wavre/Waterloo) — the booklet",
    "already describes this ('only XVI-A1 ... is put into the deck. Once",
    "Ligny is played, ... played in succession after it'), so it is still one",
    "onCampaignRounds entry, listing all four card ids.",
    "",
    "CS VI's InG round VI-4 is 'Grand Review at Boulogne (convert arms of",
    "honor to Legion of Honor)' per this sheet, which is also the event the",
    "booklet calls the trigger for LoH benefits ('after InG VI-4'). The Rules",
    "Summary Sheet separately calls the Marechal-rank unlock 'Creation of the",
    "Marshalate (Card 31)' — very likely the same physical card under its",
    "historical name, but this is a flagged open question, not certain.",
    "",
    "noPrisonerExchange on CS XV covers the CS XIV/XV transition: the",
    "booklet says 'NOT during CS XV' and this sheet separately notes 'no",
    "prisoner exchange at end of Campaign Season XIV' for the same Segment",
    "transition (Prisoner Exchange runs at the start of the Segment leading",
    "into a season, so both phrasings describe the identical event)."
  ],
